{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Open-Vocabulary Vision \u2014 CLIP Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: A tiny two-tower model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Real CLIP is ViT + transformer. For this lesson the towers are small MLPs over pre-extracted features so the training signal is visible on CPU."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class TwoTower(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, img_in=128, txt_in=64, emb=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.image_proj = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(img_in, 128), nn.ReLU(), nn.Linear(128, emb))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.text_proj = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(txt_in, 128), nn.ReLU(), nn.Linear(128, emb))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.logit_scale = nn.Parameter(torch.ones([]) * 2.6592)  # ln(1/0.07)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, img_feats, txt_feats):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        i = F.normalize(self.image_proj(img_feats), dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t = F.normalize(self.text_proj(txt_feats), dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return i, t, self.logit_scale.exp()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two projections, shared-dim output, learned temperature. Same shape as the real CLIP API."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Contrastive loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def clip_loss(image_emb, text_emb, logit_scale):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    N = image_emb.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sim = logit_scale * image_emb @ text_emb.T"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    targets = torch.arange(N, device=sim.device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    l_i = F.cross_entropy(sim, targets)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    l_t = F.cross_entropy(sim.T, targets)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return (l_i + l_t) / 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Symmetric. Higher logit_scale = sharper softmax = more confident but risk of instability."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Zero-shot classifier"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@torch.no_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def zero_shot_classify(model, image_feats, class_text_feats, class_names):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    image_feats:      (N, img_in)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    class_text_feats: (C, txt_in)   one averaged embedding per class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    i = F.normalize(model.image_proj(image_feats), dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    t = F.normalize(model.text_proj(class_text_feats), dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sim = i @ t.T"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred = sim.argmax(dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [class_names[p] for p in pred.tolist()]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One line per step. This is the exact zero-shot procedure used with a production CLIP checkpoint."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Sanity check"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "torch.manual_seed(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = TwoTower()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "img = torch.randn(8, 128)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "txt = torch.randn(8, 64)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "i, t, scale = model(img, txt)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "loss = clip_loss(i, t, scale)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"batch size: {i.size(0)}   loss: {loss.item():.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Loss should be close to `log(N) = log(8) = 2.08` for a randomly initialised model \u2014 the symmetric cross-entropy target when no structure is learned yet."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Use a pretrained OpenCLIP ViT-B/32 and do zero-shot classification on CIFAR-10 with the 80-template prompt set. Report top-1 accuracy; it should be around 85-90%.\n2. **(Medium)** Compare single-template (\"a photo of a {}\") vs 80-template averaged embeddings on the same CIFAR-10 task. Quantify the gap and explain why templates help.\n3. **(Hard)** Build a zero-shot image retrieval index: embed 1,000 images with CLIP, build a FAISS index, query with a natural language description. Report retrieval recall@5 for 20 held-out queries you write by hand."
      ]
    }
